WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.793
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Daniel. Welcome to Online Upper-Intermediate.

2
00:00:05.093 --> 00:00:08.398
Hi! I'm Nita. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.698 --> 00:00:14.241
Unit twelve: Learning for Life. In this unit, you will talk about education and lifelong learning.

4
00:00:15.250 --> 00:00:16.390
lifelong learner.

5
00:00:17.090 --> 00:00:20.332
lifelong learner means a person who keeps learning throughout life.

6
00:00:20.632 --> 00:00:24.838
My grandfather is a lifelong learner: he started English at seventy.

7
00:00:25.538 --> 00:00:27.911
Your turn. Say: lifelong learner.

8
00:00:30.611 --> 00:00:31.984
lifelong learner.

9
00:00:32.983 --> 00:00:33.996
curiosity.

10
00:00:34.696 --> 00:00:37.915
curiosity means a strong wish to know or learn something.

11
00:00:38.215 --> 00:00:40.632
Curiosity is the starting point of all learning.

12
00:00:41.332 --> 00:00:43.799
Your turn. Say: curiosity.

13
00:00:46.499 --> 00:00:47.628
curiosity.

14
00:00:48.617 --> 00:00:49.595
self-taught.

15
00:00:50.295 --> 00:00:53.339
self-taught means having learned something without a teacher.

16
00:00:53.639 --> 00:00:55.464
He's a self-taught guitarist.

17
00:00:56.164 --> 00:00:58.608
Your turn. Say: self-taught.

18
00:01:01.308 --> 00:01:02.483
self-taught.

19
00:01:03.483 --> 00:01:04.693
online degree.

20
00:01:05.393 --> 00:01:09.076
online degree means a university qualification studied on the internet.

21
00:01:09.376 --> 00:01:11.945
She earned an online degree while working full-time.

22
00:01:12.645 --> 00:01:15.286
Your turn. Say: online degree.

23
00:01:17.986 --> 00:01:19.242
online degree.

24
00:01:20.250 --> 00:01:21.042
tuition.

25
00:01:21.742 --> 00:01:24.276
tuition means teaching, or the money paid for it.

26
00:01:24.576 --> 00:01:27.260
University tuition is getting more expensive.

27
00:01:27.960 --> 00:01:30.346
Your turn. Say: tuition.

28
00:01:33.046 --> 00:01:33.896
tuition.

29
00:01:34.883 --> 00:01:35.850
academic.

30
00:01:36.550 --> 00:01:40.082
academic means related to schools, universities and study.

31
00:01:40.382 --> 00:01:42.416
Her academic results were excellent.

32
00:01:43.116 --> 00:01:45.408
Your turn. Say: academic.

33
00:01:48.108 --> 00:01:49.168
academic.

34
00:01:50.183 --> 00:01:51.498
vocational training.

35
00:01:52.198 --> 00:01:57.030
vocational training means education for a specific job, like mechanics or cooking.

36
00:01:57.330 --> 00:02:00.700
Vocational training helps young people find jobs quickly.

37
00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:04.458
Your turn. Say: vocational training.

38
00:02:07.158 --> 00:02:08.740
vocational training.

39
00:02:09.750 --> 00:02:10.832
apprenticeship.

40
00:02:11.532 --> 00:02:14.902
apprenticeship means learning a trade by working with an expert.

41
00:02:15.202 --> 00:02:17.886
He did a three-year apprenticeship as an electrician.

42
00:02:18.586 --> 00:02:21.216
Your turn. Say: apprenticeship.

43
00:02:23.916 --> 00:02:25.137
apprenticeship.

44
00:02:26.150 --> 00:02:28.231
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:28.531 --> 00:02:32.133
My cousin, whose grades weren't great, chose vocational training.

46
00:02:33.417 --> 00:02:36.452
That's a smart choice. Which trade is he learning?

47
00:02:37.750 --> 00:02:42.188
He's doing an apprenticeship with a chef, whose restaurant is in Siem Reap.

48
00:02:43.483 --> 00:02:46.600
Excellent. Not everyone needs an academic path.

49
00:02:47.917 --> 00:02:52.134
And my aunt, who is fifty, is doing an online degree!

50
00:02:53.450 --> 00:02:56.741
A true lifelong learner. Curiosity has no age limit.

51
00:02:58.050 --> 00:03:01.269
Grammar focus: Relative clauses (advanced).

52
00:03:01.569 --> 00:03:06.273
Use whose for possession, and preposition plus which or whom in formal English.

53
00:03:06.573 --> 00:03:08.770
Which can also refer to a whole idea.

54
00:03:09.070 --> 00:03:15.403
For example: The student whose project won is from Battambang. She passed every exam, which surprised everyone.

55
00:03:15.703 --> 00:03:21.197
In formal English, put the preposition before which or whom: the person to whom I spoke.

56
00:03:22.183 --> 00:03:25.149
Now read and listen. Never Too Late to Learn.

57
00:03:25.449 --> 00:03:29.109
In the past, education was something that ended when you left school.

58
00:03:30.417 --> 00:03:35.284
Today, lifelong learners take online degrees and short courses throughout their lives.

59
00:03:36.583 --> 00:03:42.170
Vocational training and apprenticeships, which were once seen as second choices, are now highly valued.

60
00:03:43.483 --> 00:03:46.412
Employers want workers whose skills are up to date.

61
00:03:47.717 --> 00:03:51.295
Curiosity, not age, is the most important requirement for learning.

62
00:03:52.583 --> 00:03:54.853
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

63
00:03:55.153 --> 00:03:57.547
Having learned something without a teacher is blank.

64
00:03:57.847 --> 00:04:01.709
A, self-taught. B, academic. C, apprenticeship.

65
00:04:05.717 --> 00:04:07.832
The answer is A: self-taught.

66
00:04:09.317 --> 00:04:11.850
The man blank car was stolen called the police.

67
00:04:12.150 --> 00:04:15.258
A, who. B, whose. C, which.

68
00:04:19.250 --> 00:04:21.191
The answer is B: whose.

69
00:04:22.683 --> 00:04:24.857
The school blank I studied has closed.

70
00:04:25.157 --> 00:04:28.184
A, at which. B, which. C, whose.

71
00:04:32.183 --> 00:04:33.997
The answer is A: at which.

72
00:04:35.483 --> 00:04:38.400
Learning a trade by working with an expert is an blank.

73
00:04:38.700 --> 00:04:42.110
A, online degree. B, apprenticeship. C, tuition.

74
00:04:46.117 --> 00:04:48.441
The answer is B: apprenticeship.

75
00:04:49.950 --> 00:04:53.494
According to the text, what is the most important requirement for learning?

76
00:04:53.794 --> 00:04:56.692
A, money. B, age. C, curiosity.

77
00:05:00.683 --> 00:05:02.613
The answer is C: curiosity.

78
00:05:04.117 --> 00:05:07.651
Now it's your turn to speak. What would you like to learn next, and why?

79
00:05:12.951 --> 00:05:18.898
I'd like to learn graphic design, which would help me in my job, and I'll probably take an online course.

80
00:05:19.198 --> 00:05:20.722
Excellent answer, Nita!

81
00:05:21.717 --> 00:05:25.809
Great work today! You learned eight new words and relative clauses (advanced).

82
00:05:26.109 --> 00:05:29.318
Today's value is pride in learning. Be proud of what you learned.

83
00:05:29.618 --> 00:05:32.305
See you in Unit thirteen. Goodbye!

84
00:05:32.605 --> 00:05:35.304
Thank you, Mr. Daniel! Bye, everyone!

